’ll kip on the sofabed."],"id":"wikt:kip:verb:13","pos":"verb","src":"wikt","sym":"18:1,49:1","syn":[],"tags":["UK","informal"]},{"def":"To snatch; take up hastily; filch","dna16":"8800077185001420","ex":[],"id":"wikt:kip:verb:14","pos":"verb","src":"wikt","sym":"","syn":[],"tags":["Northern-England","Scotland","dialectal","transitive"]},{"def":"To conduct oneself; act","dna16":"8800077185001529","ex":[],"id":"wikt:kip:verb:15","pos":"verb","src":"wikt","sym":"","syn":[],"tags":["Northern-England","dialectal","intransitive"]},{"def":"A unit of force equal to 1000 pounds-force (lbf) (4.44822 kilonewtons or 4448.22 newtons); occasionally called the kilopound.","dna16":"8800077185001628","ex":[],"id":"wikt:kip:noun:16","pos":"noun","src":"wikt","sym":"19:1,125:2","syn":[]},{"def":"A unit of weight, used, for example, to calculate shipping charges, equal to half a US ton, or 1000 pounds.","dna16":"8800077185001727","ex":[],"id":"wikt:kip:noun:17","pos":"noun","src":"wikt","sym":"38:1","syn":[]},{"def":"A unit of mass equal to 1000 avoirdupois pounds.","dna16":"8800077185001826","ex":[],"id":"wikt:kip:noun:18","pos":"noun","src":"wikt","sym":"","syn":[],"tags":["nonstandard","rare"]},{"def":"The unit of currency in Laos, divided into 100 att, symbol ₭, abbreviation LAK.","dna16":"8800077185001925","ex":[],"id":"wikt:kip:noun:19","pos":"noun","src":"wikt","sym":"","syn":[]},{"def":"A piece of flat wood used to throw the coins in a game of two-up.","dna16":"8800077185002022","ex":[],"id":"wikt:kip:noun:20","pos":"noun","src":"wikt","sym":"","syn":[],"tags":["Australia"]},{"def":"A basic skill or maneuver in artistic gymnastics on the uneven bars, parallel bars, high bar and still rings used, for example, as a way of mounting the bar in a front support position, or achieving a handstand from a hanging position. In its basic form, the legs are swung forward and upward by bending the hips, then suddenly down again, which gives the upward impulse to the body.","dna16":"8800077